{
  "case": "G37",
  "rule": "a screw head, a nut, or a washer under either, must bear on material: the fraction of its bearing annulus on the face's material, a fit warning below 50 %, a fit error on nothing (§4.5, §5.5)",
  "design": "An M8 socket head (dk 13) centred on a 40x40's c8 groove (opening 8.2), over its Ø9 hole, bears only on the lips: 45.87 %, a fit warning. A washer (d2 16) under it: 53.74 %. An M4 head (dk 7) lies wholly over the opening: a fit error. On a 50 x 10 flat face: 100 %. Bolted through two 40x40s, the hex head and the nut (s 13) each bear 45.87 %, two warnings; with two washers, one under each, 53.74 %",
